    31	## What composition is NOT proved
    32	
    33	1. **No model holds signatures and time together.** The ProVerif models represent no time. The temporal TLA+
    34	   model abstracts "signature checks … as passing" (`tla/P5P6_TemporalRevocation.tla:54-56`). So no model shows that
    35	   one receipt meets C1–C3 and C5 at once. The only joins are L-05 and L-19, both prose (table above).
    36	2. **"The signatures existed by T" is not modelled.** The signature-inclusive anchor (`A_sig`) is an assumption
    37	   on both sides (`docs/V1-CONTRACT.md:90`).
    38	3. **Terms are not bytes.** In ProVerif "the same bytes" means "the same term" (`suite/s-p1/READING-AIDS.md:257-259`).
    39	   The byte link is P8: a prose proof plus vectors, not machine-checked (`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:203-204`).
    40	4. **The capstone composes ProVerif families only.** It stays open: the author deferred two routed questions on
    41	   2026-10-07 (`suite/capstone/RESULTS.md:5`), and "Nothing below is discharged by this file"
    42	   (`suite/capstone/RESULTS.md:627-628`).
    43	5. **No model at all** for G6 (UTC bound), G7's window endpoints, or concrete DNSSEC and git authority
    44	   (`docs/V1-CONTRACT.md:98-99`); none for P9 (`COVERAGE-MAP.md:32`).
    45	6. **n = 2 is enumerated, not generalized** (`suite/s-p1/READING-AIDS.md:346-348`).
