    43	## A3.0 What forced this amendment
    44	
    45	Amendment 2 closed the clock question and left named residues.
    46	Governance review then surfaced that "attestation survives Tessera's
    47	termination" was a stated goal with no registered mechanism, and the
    48	P1 modeling kickoff forced two questions any symbolic statement of
    49	integrity depends on: what exactly Tessera attests, and what minimum
    50	evidence a valid verdict may rest on. Those questions were ruled on
    51	2026-07-28 and 2026-08-07; this amendment registers the rulings,
    52	closes or disposes the A2 residues, and adds the survivability
    53	obligations. Under A1.2's change discipline, tightenings and additions
    54	require amendment; §A3.10 states what changed, what did not, and why
    55	the A1.1 falsifier is not triggered.
