   100	## A3.2 Evidence floors: the A1.2.1 tightening
   101	
   102	**Adopted core (2026-08-07, commit 68b581c — adoption route (b): the
   103	minimal requirement adopted, its normative security boundary supplied
   104	here while the realizing mechanism remains open):**
   105	
   106	> Every valid verdict requires at least one continuous accepted
   107	> evidentiary chain per independently evaluated attestation layer;
   108	> redundant paths may be waived, but the final complete chain may not
   109	> be.
   110	
   111	**Normative expansion (the mapping clause).** "Continuous accepted
   112	evidentiary chain" means **exactly** the following witness chain, and
   113	nothing weaker:
   114	
   115	> accepted external authority evidence
   116	> → the exact authority statement consumed from the manifest
   117	> → issuer identity and signing key
   118	> → proof of possession **by that same key**
   119	> → accepted signature verifying under that key
   120	> → the exact framed bytes
   121	
   122	Both forms are registered — the sentence is the property statement the
   123	relying-party story and the written proof carry; the chain is the
   124	proof obligation the capstone (§A3.3) discharges. The mapping clause
   125	binds them: neither may drift from the other. (Author ruling
   126	2026-08-07: the two formulations are complementary altitudes, not
   127	rivals; the rationale — report what was done, defer interpretation to
   128	future verifiers and their risk tolerance — is on the record in the
   129	2026-07-28 ruling doc.)
   130	
   131	**Why linked, not counted (registered rationale).** Counted floors
   132	("≥1 accepted signature AND ≥1 accepted external evidence") admit the
   133	two-worlds attack: evidence supports manifest M′ while the accepted
   134	signature claims authority from M; both counters pass with the chain
   135	broken — the aTLS genus. And without any floor, the model's
   136	IssuanceEvent correspondence becomes privileged historical knowledge
   137	unavailable to a real verifier: the proof would be of the wrong model.
   138	
   139	**Interaction with the A1.2.1 waiver lattice (tightening, stated
   140	exactly):**
   141	
   142	1. A1.2.1's waivable item "accepting fewer than all external
   143	   manifest-authority evidences (P10)" is tightened to: **fewer, but
   144	   never zero** — redundant members of the A1.5 evidence set may be
   145	   waived; the final complete chain may not be broken or eliminated.
   146	2. **Unavailability is not waiver.** If every external authority
   147	   evidence for a layer is unavailable, unsupported, or otherwise
   148	   unperformable, the layer's verdict is `UNVERIFIABLE` — never
   149	   `VALID_DEGRADED`. Evidence that is present and whose validation is
   150	   performed but fails yields `INVALID`. The P4 partition applies
   151	   inside the floor exactly as A1.2.1 already requires of
   152	   non-waivable checks.
   153	3. **Proof of possession is chain-internal:** the possession proof
   154	   must be by the same key whose signature is accepted (consistent
   155	   with A1.5's rule that the self-signature is never an authority
    25	
