    20	## What this document is for, and what it is not
    21	
    22	This is the one place an implementer of the V1 verifier or issuer can read what V1 requires. It lists the
    23	requirements, and each one points to where it was decided (source section and rule name; line numbers are
    24	locators only, section 0). Together with A9 and ENCODING-V1 it is intended to be **sufficient with the frozen
    25	catalog, the authenticated trust configuration and the pinned normative dependencies**; those external immutable
    26	inputs do not disappear. [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F17, r2-14.2] *(Dated correction 2026-10-14: previously "each one
    27	points to the line where it was decided"; that overstated it where a requirement points only to a later owner tag.)*
    28	
    29	It is mostly an extraction. Where a rule is already decided, the source is tagged. Where it is not, the gap is
    30	marked `OPEN` and says what must be decided. It also records a small number of **new** choices that no source makes;
    31	each is labelled `OWNER PROFILE DECISION 2026-10-13`, is listed in section 0.1, and is not an A9 citation. It does not restate the byte encoding: for that, read
    32	`formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md`. It does not hold operating numbers (window dates, stop margins, hardware): those are in
    33	`docs/V1-OPERATIONS-RUNBOOK.md` and are not profile rules. It is not the 2929-line spec, which stays as the design
    34	reference and is synced after V1.
