   397	**Cross-model correspondence (the two-formalisms risk, named).** The
   398	construction is formalized twice — a TLA+ state machine and a symbolic
   399	protocol model — and two formalisms of "the same" system can quietly
   400	describe two subtly different systems, each verified, neither wrong,
   401	jointly meaningless. The informal written proof must therefore include an
   402	explicit **correspondence mapping** between the TLA+ transitions and the
   403	symbolic tool's rules/facts, arguing that both describe the same
   404	construction; the model-derived conformance vectors (A1.7) test both
   405	against the same implementation, which bounds — but does not eliminate —
   406	the divergence risk.
